IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `cat-part2-div2-3-microchip-sterilise`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 3, MANAGEMENT OF CATS (ss 26-41), with Cat
-- Regulations 2012 regs 20-25. The breeding-approval fee (Sch 3 item 4) is
-- in cat-regs-sch3-fees.l4.
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 349-465; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 208-235.

§ `Part 3 — Management of cats`

§§ `Division 1 — Cat control notices`

§§§ `26. Cat control notice may be given to cat owner`

-- s 26(1): "A local government may give a cat control notice to a person who
-- is the owner of a cat ordinarily kept in its district." A power.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 26(1)
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      lg  IS A STRING
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` d `,` lg `may give` p `a cat control notice for` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND cat's `district where ordinarily kept` EQUALS lg

-- s 26(2): "A cat control notice is to — (a) be in the form prescribed
-- [reg 20: Form 3]; and (b) identify the cat or cats ... and indicate where
-- the cat or cats are, or are suspected to be; and (c) direct the person ...
-- to comply with a provision of this Act, the regulations or a local law in
-- respect of the cat or cats; and (d) specify the period within which the
-- person to whom it is given is to comply with the notice."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 26(2); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 20
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 26(2) — what a cat control notice is to do` MEANS
    LIST "(a) be in the form prescribed — Form 3 (reg 20)"
       , "(b) identify the cat or cats in respect of which the notice is given and indicate where the cat or cats are, or are suspected to be"
       , "(c) direct the person to whom the notice is given to comply with a provision of this Act, the regulations or a local law in respect of the cat or cats"
       , "(d) specify the period within which the person to whom it is given is to comply with the notice"

§§ `Division 2 — Seizing cats`

§§§ `27. Cats may be seized`

-- s 27: "An authorised person may — (a) in any public place, seize any cat
-- that the authorised person believes, or suspects, on reasonable grounds
-- is the subject of an offence against this Act; or (b) in any premises
-- lawfully entered by the authorised person, seize any cat — (i) at the
-- request, or with the consent, of the person who is, or appears to be, the
-- owner or occupier of the premises; or (ii) under a warrant issued under
-- Part 4 Division 3 Subdivision 3."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 27
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
      s IS A Seizure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27 permits` o `to make` s IF
        `an authorised person` o
    AND (    "(a)" ... `in a public place, on a reasonable belief`
         OR  "(b)" ... `in premises lawfully entered, by consent or under warrant`)
    WHERE
        `in a public place, on a reasonable belief` MEANS
                s's `place` EQUALS `a public place`
            AND s's `believes or suspects on reasonable grounds the cat is the subject of an offence`
        `in premises lawfully entered, by consent or under warrant` MEANS
                s's `place` EQUALS `premises lawfully entered`
            AND (    "(i)"  ... s's `at the request or with the consent of the owner or occupier`
                 OR  "(ii)" ... s's `under a warrant issued under Part 4 Division 3 Subdivision 3`)

§§§ `28. Disposing of seized cats`

-- s 28: "An authorised person is to ensure that a cat seized is — (a) taken
-- to its owner; or (b) impounded in a cat management facility."
DECLARE `What became of a seized cat` IS ONE OF
    `taken to its owner`
    `impounded in a facility`  HAS `the facility` IS A Facility
    `something else`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 28
GIVEN w IS A `What became of a seized cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28 is complied with by` w IF
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `taken to its owner`        THEN TRUE                                   -- (a)
    WHEN `impounded in a facility` f THEN `a cat management facility` f          -- (b)
    WHEN `something else`            THEN FALSE

§§ `Division 3 — Dealing with cats at cat management facilities`

§§§ `29. Application of Division`

-- s 29: "This Division does not apply to a cat kept temporarily at a cat
-- management facility at the request of its owner."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 29
GIVEN stay IS A `Facility stay`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 3 applies to` stay IF
    NOT stay's `kept temporarily at the owner's request`

§§§ `30. Obligation to identify a cat's owner`

-- s 30(1): "If the identity of the owner of a cat entering a cat management
-- facility is unknown to the operator of the facility, then, as soon as
-- practicable after the cat enters the facility the operator must make every
-- reasonable attempt to identify the owner of the cat including, where
-- possible, by scanning the cat."
-- s 30(2): "Despite subsection (1), a person does not have to scan a cat if
-- — (a) the cat behaves aggressively towards the person or any other person;
-- and (b) the person believes on reasonable grounds that there is a danger
-- to the health or safety of any person in attempting to scan the cat."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 30
GIVEN stay IS A `Facility stay`
      a    IS AN `Identification attempt`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1) is contravened during` stay `by` a IF
        `the law is encoded for` (stay's `date the cat entered`)
    AND `Division 3 applies to` stay
    AND NOT stay's `operator knew the owner on entry`
    AND (    NOT a's `made every reasonable attempt as soon as practicable`
         OR  `did not scan where possible, and (2) does not excuse it`)
    WHERE
        `did not scan where possible, and (2) does not excuse it` MEANS
                a's `scanning was possible`
            AND NOT a's `scanned the cat`
            AND NOT "(2)" ... `aggressive and dangerous to scan`
        `aggressive and dangerous to scan` MEANS
                "(a)" ... a's `the cat behaved aggressively`
            AND "(b)" ... a's `believed on reasonable grounds scanning was dangerous`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 30(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `31. Cat owner liable to pay costs to cat management facility`

-- s 31(1): "The owner of a cat kept at a cat management facility is liable
-- to pay to the operator of the facility the reasonable costs associated
-- with any of the following that have been incurred in relation to the cat
-- — (a) removing and impounding the cat; (b) keeping and caring for the cat;
-- (c) the implantation of a microchip in the cat under section 33; (d) the
-- sterilisation of the cat under section 33; (e) the destruction and the
-- disposal of the cat under section 34." Whether a cost was "reasonable" is
-- a judgement: the inputs are the reasonable costs. s 31(2): recoverable in
-- a court of competent jurisdiction.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 31(1)
GIVEN stay  IS A `Facility stay`
      costs IS A `Facility costs`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the costs the owner is liable to pay for` stay `:` costs MEANS
    IF   `Division 3 applies to` stay
    THEN     costs's `removing and impounding the cat`                      -- (a)
        PLUS costs's `keeping and caring for the cat`                       -- (b)
        PLUS costs's `implanting a microchip under section 33`              -- (c)
        PLUS costs's `sterilising the cat under section 33`                 -- (d)
        PLUS costs's `destroying and disposing of the cat under section 34` -- (e)
    ELSE 0

§§§ `32. Notice to be given to cat's owner, if identified`

-- s 32: "If the operator of a cat management facility knows the identity of
-- the owner of a cat kept at the facility then the operator is to take all
-- reasonable steps to ensure that the owner of the cat is notified in
-- writing — (a) of the name and address of the cat management facility where
-- the cat is being kept; and (b) that the cat may be re-housed, offered for
-- sale or destroyed if the cat is not reclaimed by its owner within the
-- holding period specified in the notice (that is not to be less than 7
-- working days from the notice being given); and (c) of the costs that the
-- owner may be liable for under section 31; and (d) where relevant, that
-- under section 33 — (i) the cat is to be microchipped, unless it is proved
-- ... that the cat is exempt from microchipping ...; (ii) that the cat is to
-- be sterilised, unless it is proved ... that the cat is exempt from
-- sterilisation ...".
--
-- "where relevant" in (d) is read as: (i) is relevant when the operator
-- believes the cat is not microchipped, (ii) when it believes it is not
-- sterilised — the beliefs that open s 33. Both are inputs.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 32
GIVEN n IS A `Section 32 notice`
      `the cat is believed not microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cat is believed not sterilised`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what the s 32 notice` n `lacks, where microchipping is relevant:` `the cat is believed not microchipped` `and sterilisation:` `the cat is believed not sterilised` MEANS
    concat (LIST `(a)`, `(b)`, `the holding period`, `(c)`, `(d)(i)`, `(d)(ii)`)
    WHERE
        `missing` label holds MEANS IF holds THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST label
        `(a)` MEANS `missing` "(a) the name and address of the facility" (n's `states the facility's name and address`)
        `(b)` MEANS `missing` "(b) that the cat may be re-housed, offered for sale or destroyed" (n's `states the cat may be re-housed, offered for sale or destroyed if not reclaimed`)
        `the holding period` MEANS `missing` "(b) a holding period of not less than 7 working days" (n's `holding period specified, in working days` AT LEAST 7)
        `(c)` MEANS `missing` "(c) the costs the owner may be liable for under section 31" (n's `states the costs the owner may be liable for under s 31`)
        `(d)(i)` MEANS `missing` "(d)(i) that the cat is to be microchipped" ((NOT `the cat is believed not microchipped`) OR n's `states the cat is to be microchipped unless shown exempt`)
        `(d)(ii)` MEANS `missing` "(d)(ii) that the cat is to be sterilised" ((NOT `the cat is believed not sterilised`) OR n's `states the cat is to be sterilised unless shown exempt`)

-- The offence: the operator knew the owner, and did not take all
-- reasonable steps to notify a notice that says everything s 32 requires.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 32
GIVEN stay IS A `Facility stay`
      `took all reasonable steps to notify the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice lacks something`                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32 is contravened during` stay `, steps taken:` `took all reasonable steps to notify the owner` `, notice lacking:` `the notice lacks something` IF
        `Division 3 applies to` stay
    AND `the operator knows the owner`
    AND ((NOT `took all reasonable steps to notify the owner`) OR `the notice lacks something`)
    WHERE
        `the operator knows the owner` MEANS
            stay's `operator knew the owner on entry`
            OR CONSIDER stay's `date the owner was identified`
               WHEN JUST x  THEN TRUE
               WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 32 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 32 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `33. Operator of cat management facility may have cat microchipped and sterilised`

-- s 33: "If the operator of a cat management facility — (a) believes on
-- reasonable grounds that a cat kept at the facility is not microchipped,
-- and has no reason to believe that the cat is exempt from microchipping as
-- referred to in section 14(2); or (b) believes on reasonable grounds that a
-- cat kept at the facility is not sterilised, and has no reason to believe
-- that the cat is exempt from sterilisation as referred to in section 18(2),
-- then the operator ... may do anything necessary to ensure that the cat is
-- microchipped or sterilised, or both, as is relevant, before the cat is
-- reclaimed or otherwise transferred from that facility." Beliefs are inputs.
DECLARE `Section 33 permission` HAS
    `may have the cat microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN    -- (a)
    `may have the cat sterilised`   IS A BOOLEAN    -- (b)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 33
GIVEN stay IS A `Facility stay`
      `believes on reasonable grounds it is not microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has reason to believe it is exempt from microchipping` IS A BOOLEAN
      `believes on reasonable grounds it is not sterilised`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `has reason to believe it is exempt from sterilisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 33 permission`
`what s 33 permits during` stay `:` `believes on reasonable grounds it is not microchipped` `,` `has reason to believe it is exempt from microchipping` `,` `believes on reasonable grounds it is not sterilised` `,` `has reason to believe it is exempt from sterilisation` MEANS
    `Section 33 permission` WITH
        `may have the cat microchipped` IS     `Division 3 applies to` stay
                                           AND "(a)" ... `believes on reasonable grounds it is not microchipped`
                                           AND NOT `has reason to believe it is exempt from microchipping`
        `may have the cat sterilised`   IS     `Division 3 applies to` stay
                                           AND "(b)" ... `believes on reasonable grounds it is not sterilised`
                                           AND NOT `has reason to believe it is exempt from sterilisation`

§§§ `34. Dealing with unidentified and unclaimed cats`

-- s 34(1): "If — (a) the operator of a cat management facility does not know
-- the identity of the owner of a cat and fails to identify the owner within
-- 3 working days of the cat entering the cat management facility; or (b)
-- the owner of a cat notified under section 32 has not reclaimed the cat
-- within — (i) 7 working days from the notice being given under that
-- section; or (ii) the holding period specified in the notice, whichever is
-- later; or (c) the owner of a cat has surrendered the cat to the cat
-- management facility, then the operator of the facility may — (d) transfer
-- the cat; or (e) cause the cat to be destroyed in a humane manner."
--
-- Working days: fork F-01 (cat-time.l4). "within 3 working days of the cat
-- entering" counts the working days after the day of entry (s 61(1)(b)); the
-- power arises once the last of them has ended.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 34(1)(a)
GIVEN stay     IS A `Facility stay`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to identify the owner of the cat in` stay `given` holidays MEANS
    `the date` 3 `working days after` (stay's `date the cat entered`) `given` holidays

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 34(1)(b)
GIVEN stay     IS A `Facility stay`
      notice   IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to reclaim the cat in` stay `after notice on` notice `given` holidays MEANS
    IF   `the end of (ii)` GREATER THAN `the end of (i)`
    THEN `the end of (ii)`
    ELSE `the end of (i)`
    WHERE
        `the end of (i)`  MEANS `the date` 7 `working days after` notice `given` holidays
        `the end of (ii)` MEANS `the date` (stay's `holding period specified in the notice, in working days`) `working days after` notice `given` holidays

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 34(1)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      stay     IS A `Facility stay`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` d `the operator may transfer or humanely destroy the cat in` stay `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `Division 3 applies to` stay
    AND (    "(a)" ... `unidentified after 3 working days`
         ..  "(b)" ... `unclaimed after notice`
         OR  "(c)" ... stay's `surrendered by the owner`)
    WHERE
        `unidentified after 3 working days` MEANS
                NOT stay's `operator knew the owner on entry`
            AND d GREATER THAN `the last day to identify the owner of the cat in` stay `given` holidays
            AND CONSIDER stay's `date the owner was identified`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                WHEN JUST x  THEN x GREATER THAN `the last day to identify the owner of the cat in` stay `given` holidays
        `unclaimed after notice` MEANS
            CONSIDER stay's `date notice given under section 32`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST n  THEN     d GREATER THAN `the last day to reclaim the cat in` stay `after notice on` n `given` holidays
                              AND `not reclaimed by` (`the last day to reclaim the cat in` stay `after notice on` n `given` holidays)
        `not reclaimed by` last MEANS
            CONSIDER stay's `date reclaimed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN r GREATER THAN last

-- s 34(2): "Despite subsection (1), the operator of a cat management
-- facility may cause any cat kept at the facility to be destroyed in a
-- humane manner immediately — (a) if the operator believes on reasonable
-- grounds that the cat — (i) is feral, diseased or dangerous; and (ii) has
-- caused or given, or is likely to cause or give, serious injury, or serious
-- illness, to a person, another animal or itself; or (b) in the
-- circumstances, if any, prescribed." No regulation under the Act prescribes
-- any circumstances for (b) (inputs/PROVENANCE.md).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 34(2)
GIVEN stay IS A `Facility stay`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator may immediately destroy the cat in` stay IF
        `Division 3 applies to` stay
    AND (    "(a)" ... `believed feral, diseased or dangerous, and injurious`
         OR  "(b) in the circumstances, if any, prescribed — none are" ... FALSE)
    WHERE
        `believed feral, diseased or dangerous, and injurious` MEANS
                "(i)"  ... stay's `operator believes the cat feral, diseased or dangerous`
            AND "(ii)" ... stay's `operator believes the cat has caused, or is likely to cause, serious injury or illness`

§§ `Division 4 — Breeding of cats`

§§§ `Subdivision 1 — Restrictions on breeding cats`

§§§§ `35. Only approved cat breeders may breed cats`

-- s 35(1): "A person must not breed cats unless the person is an approved
-- cat breeder."
-- s 35(2)-(4): on conviction the court MAY order the person's cats
-- sterilised; a copy goes to the local government; the order is enforceable
-- as a judgment. Sentencing is not modelled.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 35(1)
GIVEN p                IS A Person
      `breeds cats`    IS A BOOLEAN
      d                IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(1) is contravened by` p `, breeding:` `breeds cats` `, on` d IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `breeds cats`
    AND NOT `an approved cat breeder` p

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 35(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 35(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `Subdivision 2 — Becoming an approved cat breeder`

§§§§ `36. Application for approval to breed cats`

-- s 36(1): "The owner of a cat that is ordinarily kept in the district of a
-- local government may apply to the local government for the grant or
-- renewal of an approval to breed cats." s 36(2) and reg 21: Form 1 Parts A,
-- B, E, F and G, with the Schedule 3 item 4 fee.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 36(1)
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
      lg  IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply on` d `under s 36 by` p `, owning` cat `, to` lg IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND cat's `district where ordinarily kept` EQUALS lg

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 21(a)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 21(a) — the parts of Form 1 a breeding application supplies` MEANS
    LIST "Part A — Owner details", "Part B — Cat details", "Part E — Application for approved breeder", "Part F — Previous convictions", "Part G — Declaration"

§§§§ `37. Approval to breed cats`

-- reg 22(1): "A local government may refuse an application for the grant or
-- renewal of an approval to breed cats if the local government is satisfied
-- that an infringement notice under the Act has been issued to, and paid by,
-- the applicant within the 12 months prior to the application." This is the
-- circumstance prescribed under s 37(2)(f).
-- FORK F-15: "within the 12 months prior to the application" is read as the
-- notice having been ISSUED in those 12 months; the date of payment is not
-- given and is not tested.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 22(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an infringement notice was issued to and paid by` p `within the 12 months before` d IF
    any (GIVEN n YIELD     n's `outcome` EQUALS `paid`
                       AND `within the` 12 `months before` d `, an event on` (n's `date given`))
        (p's `infringement notices under the Act`)

-- reg 22(2): "Where a local government is satisfied that an infringement
-- notice under the Act has been issued to the applicant within the 12
-- months prior to the application, but the matter has not been resolved by
-- either payment or court proceedings, the local government may defer
-- consideration of an application ... until the matter is resolved."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 22(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unresolved infringement notice was issued to` p `within the 12 months before` d IF
    any (GIVEN n YIELD     n's `outcome` EQUALS `not yet resolved`
                       AND `within the` 12 `months before` d `, an event on` (n's `date given`))
        (p's `infringement notices under the Act`)

-- A conviction "against — (i) this Act; or (ii) the Dog Act 1976; or (iii)
-- the Animal Welfare Act 2002" within the previous 3 years — s 37(2)(d) and
-- reg 23(b). One is enough here (s 9(2)(e) and s 10(b) need two). Fork F-07
-- (only offences against the Act itself) and F-08 (counted back from the
-- day the application is determined) apply as in s 9.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 37(2)(d); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 23(b)
GIVEN p IS A Person
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `convicted within the previous 3 years of an offence against the three Acts:` p `, counted on` d IF
    any (GIVEN c YIELD     c's `instrument` EQUALS `the Act itself`
                       AND (    "(i)"   ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Cat Act 2011`
                            ..  "(ii)"  ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Dog Act 1976`
                            OR  "(iii)" ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Animal Welfare Act 2002`)
                       AND `within the` 36 `months before` d `, an event on` (c's `date of the conviction`))
        (p's `convictions`)

-- s 37(2): "A local government may refuse an application ... only if the
-- local government is satisfied that one or more of the following apply —
-- (a) the applicant is a child under 18 years of age; (b) the applicant has
-- no, or insufficient, facilities to breed cats in a safe and ethical way;
-- (c) the applicant has no, or unsuitable, premises where cats can be bred
-- in a safe and ethical way; (d) the applicant has been convicted within the
-- previous 3 years of an offence against — (i) this Act; or (ii) the Dog Act
-- 1976; or (iii) the Animal Welfare Act 2002; (e) the applicant is not a fit
-- and proper person to breed cats; (f) such other circumstances, if any, as
-- are prescribed [reg 22(1)]."
--
-- `on` is the day the test is applied: the day of determination for s 37;
-- the day of cancellation for s 38 (fork F-14). `applied` is the day of the
-- application, from which reg 22(1) counts its 12 months.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 37(2); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 22(1)
GIVEN p       IS A Person
      f       IS A `Breeding application findings`
      on      IS A DATE
      applied IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the s 37(2) things that apply to` p `, found` f `, on` on `, applied for on` applied MEANS
    concat (LIST `(a)`, `(b)`, `(c)`, `(d)`, `(e)`, `(f)`)
    WHERE
        `present` label holds MEANS IF holds THEN LIST label ELSE EMPTY
        `(a)` MEANS `present` "(a) the applicant is a child under 18 years of age" (`under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (p's `date of birth`) `, on` on)
        `(b)` MEANS `present` "(b) the applicant has no, or insufficient, facilities to breed cats in a safe and ethical way" (f's `no, or insufficient, facilities to breed cats in a safe and ethical way`)
        `(c)` MEANS `present` "(c) the applicant has no, or unsuitable, premises where cats can be bred in a safe and ethical way" (f's `no, or unsuitable, premises where cats can be bred in a safe and ethical way`)
        `(d)` MEANS `present` "(d) the applicant has been convicted within the previous 3 years of an offence against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002" (`convicted within the previous 3 years of an offence against the three Acts:` p `, counted on` on)
        `(e)` MEANS `present` "(e) the applicant is not a fit and proper person to breed cats" (f's `not a fit and proper person to breed cats`)
        `(f)` MEANS `present` "(f) reg 22(1): an infringement notice under the Act was issued to, and paid by, the applicant within the 12 months prior" (`an infringement notice was issued to and paid by` p `within the 12 months before` applied)

-- s 37(5): "Despite subsection (2), a local government is not to refuse to
-- grant or renew an approval to breed cats if the applicant belongs to a
-- class of persons prescribed for the purposes of this subsection."
-- reg 23: "... if the applicant — (a) has attained the age of 18 years; and
-- (b) has not been convicted within the previous 3 years of an offence
-- against — (i) the Cat Act 2011; or (ii) the Dog Act 1976; or (iii) the
-- Animal Welfare Act 2002; and (c) is a current member of one of the
-- following organisations — [the four cat-fancy bodies]".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 37(5); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 23
GIVEN p IS A Person
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the class reg 23 prescribes:` p `, on` d IF
        "(a)" ... NOT `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (p's `date of birth`) `, on` d
    AND "(b)" ... NOT `convicted within the previous 3 years of an offence against the three Acts:` p `, counted on` d
    AND "(c)" ... NOT null (p's `current memberships`)

DECLARE `Breeding approval determination` IS ONE OF
    `the local government may refuse to consider the application`                     -- s 37(4)
    `the local government is not to refuse the application`                           -- s 37(5), reg 23
    `the local government may defer consideration until the infringement notice is resolved`   -- reg 22(2)
    `the local government may refuse the application` HAS `the grounds` IS A LIST OF STRING      -- s 37(2)
    `the local government is to grant or renew the approval`                          -- s 37(1), no ground

-- s 37(1): "On receiving an application ... a local government is to — (a)
-- grant or refuse to grant an approval ...; or (b) renew or refuse to renew
-- an approval ...". s 37(3)-(4): the same request-for-information power as
-- s 9(5)-(6).
--
-- FORK F-13: the order of the arms. A request not complied with comes first
-- — refusing to CONSIDER is not refusing to grant, so s 37(5) does not bar
-- it. s 37(5) then comes before reg 22(2): a deferral made under a
-- regulation headed "(s. 37(2)(f))" is read as subject to "Despite
-- subsection (2)".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 37(1)-(5); Cat Regulations 2012 regs 22, 23
GIVEN app     IS A `Breeding application`
      request IS A MAYBE `Information request`
GIVETH A `Breeding approval determination`
`the s 37 determination of` app `, after the request` request MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for` d
    THEN BRANCH IF `the applicant did not comply with a request in time`
                   THEN `the local government may refuse to consider the application`
                IF `in the class reg 23 prescribes:` (app's `applicant`) `, on` d
                   THEN `the local government is not to refuse the application`
                IF `an unresolved infringement notice was issued to` (app's `applicant`) `within the 12 months before` (app's `date made`)
                   THEN `the local government may defer consideration until the infringement notice is resolved`
                IF NOT null `grounds`
                   THEN `the local government may refuse the application` `grounds`
                OTHERWISE `the local government is to grant or renew the approval`
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    WHERE
        d MEANS app's `date determined`
        `grounds` MEANS `the s 37(2) things that apply to` (app's `applicant`) `, found` (app's `findings`) `, on` d `, applied for on` (app's `date made`)
        `the applicant did not comply with a request in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER request
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN     "(3) of not more than 21 days" ... r's `days allowed` AT MOST 21
                              AND NOT r's `complied with in time`

-- s 37(6) and reg 24: "An approval to breed cats, or a renewal of approval,
-- granted under section 37 of the Act has effect for one year." A year is
-- 12 months (Interpretation Act s 5), reckoned under s 62.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 37(6); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 24
GIVEN granted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of effect of an approval granted on` granted MEANS
    `the day after a period of` 12 `months beginning on` granted MINUS 1

§§§§ `38. Cancellation of approval to breed cats`

-- s 38: "A local government may cancel an approval to breed cats if one or
-- more of the things set out in section 37(2) applies in respect of the
-- approved cat breeder." A power. s 37(5) protects only grant and renewal,
-- so it does not stand in the way of a cancellation.
-- FORK F-14: the s 37(2) things are tested on the day of cancellation, and
-- reg 22(1)'s "12 months prior to the application" as the 12 months before
-- that day.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 38
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      p IS A Person
      f IS A `Breeding application findings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` d `the local government may cancel the approval of` p `, found` f IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an approved cat breeder` p
    AND NOT null (`the s 37(2) things that apply to` p `, found` f `, on` d `, applied for on` d)

§§§§ `39. Certificate to be given to approved cat breeder`

-- s 39(1): a certificate in the prescribed form — Form 4 (reg 25). s 39(2):
-- a replacement MAY be given for one stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 39(1); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 25
GIVETH A STRING
`s 39(1) — the certificate form` MEANS "Form 4 — Certificate of approved cat breeder"

§§§§ `40. Notice to be given of certain decisions made under this Subdivision`

-- s 40(1): "Within 7 days after making a decision referred to in subsection
-- (2) the local government is to give to the person affected by the
-- decision notice in writing of — (a) the decision; and (b) the reasons for
-- the decision; and (c) the person's rights under Part 4 Division 5 ...".
-- s 40(2): "(a) refuse to approve or renew the approval of a person to breed
-- cats under section 37; or (b) cancel the approval of a person to breed
-- cats under section 38."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 40(2)
GIVEN dec IS A `Reviewable decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a decision s 40 applies to` dec IF
        "(a)" ... dec EQUALS `refusal to grant an approval to breed`
    ..  "(a)" ... dec EQUALS `refusal to renew an approval to breed`
    OR  "(b)" ... dec EQUALS `cancellation of an approval to breed`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 40(1)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 40 — the local government's duty, counted in days from the decision` MEANS
    PARTY `the local government`
    MUST  `give notice of the decision, the reasons and the rights of objection and review`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local government` BECAUSE "s 40(1): written notice of the decision, the reasons and the rights under Part 4 Division 5 was not given within 7 days after the decision"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 40(1)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      h        IS AN `Objection history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 40 notice is late, as at` d `, for` h `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `a decision s 40 applies to` (h's `decision`)
    AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (h's `date of the decision`) `, done on` (h's `date notice of the decision was given`) `, as at` d `given` holidays

§§ `Division 5 — Miscellaneous`

§§§ `41. Cats not to be offered as prizes`

-- s 41: "A person must not offer a cat as a prize in a raffle or similar
-- event or game of chance."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 41
GIVEN `offered a cat as a prize in a raffle or similar event or game of chance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 is contravened, where the person` `offered a cat as a prize in a raffle or similar event or game of chance` IF
    `offered a cat as a prize in a raffle or similar event or game of chance`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 41 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000
